From 3b3a989bd9dd7b686622db6ee9447680af0ce924 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:29:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] Give a group chat its picture, on the node rather than
 on a buddy

Contacts have had pictures all along and groups have not, because the only
sweep is over buddies and a group is deliberately not one here: a chat
cannot be messaged like a contact, and a row for one leads nowhere.

Reintroducing group buddies would be the wrong repair. libpurple attaches a
custom icon to any node in the list, chats included, and persists the file
name into blist.xml, so that is where a group's picture goes. Note that
purple_buddy_icons_set_for_user cannot serve here at all: it only keeps an
icon something takes a reference to, so for a chat it would allocate the
image, find no taker and free it again on the spot.

The Go layer needed nothing. GetProfilePictureInfo takes a JID and does not
care whether it names a person or a group.
---
 glue/blist.c           | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 glue/gowhatsapp.h      |  2 ++
 glue/presence.c        | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 glue/process_message.c |  1 +
 4 files changed, 66 insertions(+)

diff --git a/glue/blist.c b/glue/blist.c
index 568cf2f..ea47d09 100644
--- a/glue/blist.c
+++ b/glue/blist.c
@@ -88,6 +88,30 @@ void gowhatsapp_for_all_buddies(PurpleAccount *account, void(*func)(PurpleAccoun
     }
 }
 
+/*
+ * Calls a function once on each group chat of this account.
+ *
+ * The counterpart of gowhatsapp_for_all_buddies, and needed because a group is deliberately not a
+ * buddy here: a chat cannot be messaged like a contact, and a contact list row for one is a row that
+ * leads nowhere. Anything that wants to treat groups the way contacts are treated has to walk them
+ * separately, and the walk is the one gowhatsapp_find_blist_chat already does.
+ */
+void gowhatsapp_for_all_chats(PurpleAccount *account, void(*func)(PurpleAccount *, PurpleChat *)) {
+    g_return_if_fail(account != NULL);
+
+    for (PurpleBlistNode *node = purple_blist_get_root();
+         node != NULL;
+         node = purple_blist_node_next(node, TRUE)) {
+        if (PURPLE_IS_CHAT(node)) {
+            PurpleChat *chat = PURPLE_CHAT(node);
+
+            if (purple_chat_get_account(chat) == account) {
+                func(account, chat);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+
 // Group chat related functions
 
 /*
