From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:35:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] Forward incoming receipts and sent-message ids.

Incoming events.Receipt used to be logged and dropped. Now every receipt
is handed to the purple part as a new receipt message type, one call per
message ID (their order is platform dependent), with the same LID to
phone number mapping the message path applies. Successful sends report a
"sent" receipt carrying the ID the server assigned, since without it a
consumer could never match a later delivered or read receipt to the
message it confirms. The C part always emits the registered
"gowhatsapp-receipt" signal with a hash table of the details, so
front-ends and plug-ins can draw ticks; behind the new receipt-display
account option (off by default) a read receipt is also shown as a system
message in the conversation window, as suggested by the README's planned
features list.
