From c98dbaf18cd3944133196bd86b4ab1d623e67908 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 04:04:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] Ask even when no message of the conversation is known

The request points at a message and asks for what came before it, and
the message cache was the only place it looked for one. The cache holds
a few hundred messages across every conversation, so a chat nobody has
spoken in since this client started is simply not in it, and the fetch
gave up before it began: the very conversation whose history is worth
having is the one the cache has never heard of.

Such a request now points at the present moment and names no message.
Whether the phone answers that is the phone's business, and the log says
which of the two kinds of request went out, and whether an answer came,
since this is a feature whose failure is otherwise silence.

